WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.493
NubOT's key idea is to split the hard unbalanced
problem into two coupled pieces: feature

00:00:05.573 --> 00:00:07.622
transformation and mass rescaling.

00:00:07.702 --> 00:00:13.132
It introduces proxy measures that are simply
rescaled versions of the source and target,

00:00:13.212 --> 00:00:18.267
weighted by scalar fields eta and zeta, chosen so
the two proxies have equal mass.

00:00:18.347 --> 00:00:23.464
Between these now-balanced measures it solves a
standard optimal transport problem,

00:00:23.544 --> 00:00:29.100
learning forward and backward Monge maps as the
gradients of convex potentials represented

00:00:29.180 --> 00:00:31.103
by input convex neural networks.

00:00:31.183 --> 00:00:35.800
Because the marginals themselves shift as the
reweighting functions update,

00:00:35.880 --> 00:00:41.373
NubOT uses an alternating minimization: it
estimates the mass rescaling with an efficient

00:00:41.453 --> 00:00:43.815
single-step unbalanced Sinkhorn update,

00:00:43.895 --> 00:00:47.947
then updates the transport potentials through a
min-max objective,

00:00:48.027 --> 00:00:49.450
cycling between the two.

00:00:49.530 --> 00:00:53.019
The reweighting functions are learned as neural networks,

00:00:53.099 --> 00:00:59.970
so at test time the model can map a new cell and
simultaneously predict whether its mass should grow or shrink.
